    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm working on a 2022 F-150 that's having some transmission slipping issues. when i hook up the scan tool, i'm seeing a lot of irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit during the shifts. what are the most likely causes for these kinds of pressure fluctuations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular hydraulic pressure spikes during shifts in a 2022 F-150 are often caused by a failing Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid, stuck TCC/lock-up solenoid, or a faulty shift solenoid within the transmission. These electrical components can fail internally, causing the transmission control module to compensate by creating erratic pressure signals. Additionally, low transmission fluid level, degraded ATF fluid, or a failing filter can contribute to hydraulic instability and shifting complaints. It is recommended to check the scan tool for specific TCC/shift solenoid status codes and address code clarifications before replacing expensive transmission parts.",
